## How these notes are kept
This file holds only what every session needs, whatever it works on. **Keep it under 200 lines.**
- **One area's decisions are in that area's rule file** under `.claude/rules/` ("Where each area is written", below),
  with the owner's own words and dates. Replaced decisions and long accounts go to `.claude/rule-history/<area>.md`, read
  with Grep. A rule file is read into a session by itself when a file under its `paths` is opened. **Before answering
  the owner about an area, or changing anything in it, read its rule file, whether or not it was loaded.**
- **A new decision of the owner's is written into its area's rule file in the turn it is given**, with the owner's
  words and the date (the skill `record-decision`); into this file only when every session must know it. When an area's
  files move, its rule file's `paths` are changed with them.
- **A procedure with steps is a skill** under `.claude/skills/<name>/SKILL.md` ("Procedures", below).
- What is in hand, who has it and where its files are goes in the inventory, never here.

## How the work is run
The delivery flow: `.claude/rules/workflow.md` (the rules in force) and `docs/method.md` (why). In short:
- one feature in build at a time, with a fixed budget; tasks of at most a day with done-when checks that only QA passes,
  on the stage build;
- a readiness review before each start; a retrospective after each feature;
- the team is <three> sessions: lead, builder, QA<, design>; roles on the list (`node tools/feat.mjs status`);
- each piece of work states a model and an effort level; at most two helpers per session;
- show first, look before measuring, evidence not estimates; four rounds on one problem, then the owner.
- **Every tab is summarised automatically at a window of <215,000> tokens.** After a summary, before anything else: read
  your hand-over in `reports/team/handover/` and run `node tools/feat.mjs next`.

